  "verdict": "A controlled HTTP error-body stall is reproduced and repaired. The available customer reports do not establish that either encountered this condition. Neither report is closed.",
  "cause": "The response headers disarmed the connect guard, including its caller-abort forwarding, and responseErrorDetail awaited res.text() without the idle watchdog or original run signal. A non-ending error body therefore outlived cancellation and the configured body-idle interval.",
  "repair": "Read error-body chunks using the existing idleGuardedReader and original signal; propagate timeout/abort; preserve progressing error payloads and metadata. Change the loop diagnostic to describe idle expiry without asserting that no prior bytes arrived.",
  "untouched": [
    "Ollama allocation-error classification and retry path owned by the graphics lane",
    "Ollama 300000ms connect allowance",
    "Existing retry policy and native/compatible success parser",
    "Shared schema/events",
    "Trunk"
  ],
